R-RG2 R-RG7 R-RG1 R-RG8 R-AL2 R-AP16 R-DT5 R-RG4 R-IX3 (slice 225, entry `commands`): the built-in default is the registry `https://registry.roc-talon.org` (Design Q208). No flag, no TALON_REGISTRY, no `registry` in config.toml: the closure query goes to that host (the route is fx/http/registry.roc-talon.org/v1/closure.POST). The body and the answer are those of `registry/al2-update-query` run 2.
Run 1: nothing is set. The guard reads the kept answers and asks GitHub for acme/parser (R-RG4), then one POST to the default registry (R-AL2 step 2). `--json`: `"snapshot":"log:30"`. The index dir is `https_registry.roc-talon.org` (R-IX1, R-RG7 row 7, no port).
Run 2: TALON_REGISTRY=direct wins over the default (R-RG1): the direct calls of the GitHub release lists, the line `resolved at <time>`. The user who wants `direct` sets it (R-RG2).
Run 3: the same default host, written with upper case, the default port and a trailing `/` in TALON_REGISTRY: the base URL form (R-RG7 rows 2 to 5) is the same host, so the same route answers.
